# Android architecture

- `:core` is a JVM Kotlin module. Zero Android imports (`android.*`, `androidx.*` except none).
- `:app` owns Room, WorkManager, AlarmManager, notifications, Compose, Firebase.
- Unidirectional data: UI event → ViewModel/use case → `:core` engine → new `PetState` → persist → UI state.
- WorkManager for periodic reconciliation. AlarmManager only for time-critical alerts that WorkManager cannot guarantee.
- Compose screens are stateless where possible. Hold UI state in ViewModels. Navigation stays in `:app` ui.
- Background work and notification code must be testable without starting the full Activity graph.
- Main thread: no Room queries, no file I/O, no catch-up simulation loops.

Layer check: if a Composable imports `com.pipkin.core.simulation`, the boundary is already broken — inject a ViewModel instead.
